# Ownership Boundaries

## CODEOWNERS

Before modifying any file, check if a CODEOWNERS file exists at the project root.

- If the file being modified has an owner that is NOT you/your team: **REFUSE** the edit
- Explain which team owns the file and suggest they make the change
- If no CODEOWNERS file exists: all files are open (default for small teams)

## Governance Files (Never Modify Without Permission)

These files require explicit human request to modify:

- `.cursor/rules/sdlc/*` — overlay governance rules
- `.copier-answers.sdlc.yml` — overlay configuration
- `.sdlc/trust-ledger.json` — trust scoring
- `.sdlc/KILLSWITCH` — only humans create/remove this
- `AGENTS.md` — agent instructions (suggest edits, don't apply)

## Cross-Module Boundaries

If the project has clear module boundaries (packages/, services/, apps/):

- Stay within the module relevant to the current task
- If a change requires touching another module, flag it and ask
- Never make "while I'm here" improvements in adjacent modules

## Verification Command

After any edit, confirm the change doesn't break anything: `make verify`
